[Music]  foreign  in the past decade no politician has  probably been more influential  in shifting china's climate policy than  xi jinhua  as china's lead negotiator at the united  nations climate change conferences  he's been critical to forging climate  agreements on the international stage  now he's a special adviser to china's  environmental ministry  and the head of a leading institute for  climate and sustainability research  a study done by that institute  contributed to china's decision to be  carbon neutral by 2060  so how is china going to achieve its  carbon neutrality goals in time  and what role will this climate veteran  continue to play  after working for china's environmental  protection ministry for almost a decade  shir was appointed as its head in 1993.  during cs tenor at the environmental  protection ministry  a management system for major air and  water pollutants were put in place  and in addition environmental targets  started to be included  in china's five-year plans these  blueprints for economic and social  development  which had previously been very focused  on economic growth  he resigned in 2005 after a series of  chemical plant explosions in china's  jilim province  the explosions were caused by the  improper storage of dangerous chemicals  and left six dead and dozens injured  a local river was also polluted by  leaked chemicals  and tens of thousands of residents had  to be evacuated his resignation came  as the environmental agency criticized  local officials for covering up the  accident  and for this blind pursuit of economic  development  which damaged china's environment but  the resignation appeared to be only a  blip in his career  and asia later assumed the role of vice  chairman of the national development  and reform commission at the time the  ndrc china's top  economic planner was responsible for  making environmental policy  social continued to have a leading role  in china's climate strategies  in 2007 shia was appointed as china's  lead climate negotiator at the un  climate change conferences by then four  decades of breakneck economic  growth had turned china into the world's  biggest carbon emitter  steadily though the country's stance has  shifted from defending its right to emit  to promoting low carbon development as a  national strategy  [Music]  [Music]  in china's policy making system it's  difficult to point to the role of the  individual person  but we know that sia played quite an  important role in proposing ambitious  climate targets for china  which were eventually adopted by the  country's top leaders  so the advantages that sia had is that  he is very well versed  in sort of the party structure and the  party priorities  as well as international climate  priorities so he knows how to translate  the international pressures into better  chinese policies  [Music]  [Applause]  is known as a very candid tough  negotiator  in international climate talks at the  durban talks in 2011  a video cia repeatedly banging a table  over what he believed  were hypocritical demands by developed  countries  was widely broadcast in china and yet  his counterparts continued to speak to a  sense of humor  and his general likability  foreign  beyond the negotiating table shia has a  personal commitment to fight for change  after traveling to parts of the world  affected by the climate crisis  so  [Music]  in 2017 received a 2.5 million  award for his efforts to tackle climate  change he donated the money to his alma  mater  chingua university hoping to encourage  the next generation of climate leaders  he's now the head of the university's  institute of climate change and  sustainable development  and his team's research has helped set  china's goal to become carbon neutral  by 2060. we are already seeing some  suggestions for how to make this happen  so one climate institute that works with  cs institute at xinhua  has laid out a plan of increasing  renewable and nuclear energy  and completely phasing out coal power  the plan entails a very gradual  transition over the next 15 years  with a rapid acceleration after 2035  so under this particular plan coal-fired  electricity would be eliminated by 2050  and china's energy mix would undergo a  dramatic transformation  we've also seen these estimates that  something like 15 trillion dollars will  need to be invested  over the next 30 years to meet these  targets  [Music]  since  [Music]  tensions between the u.s and china have  been rising in recent years  and the u.s government has withdrawn  from the paris agreement  but shir is convinced there's no time to  lose  bye  you

